ach solvent  tested for each sample  again we have our percent difference on  our y-axis  and our sample number on the x-axis  um mtbe data was replaced with the most  recent of data  um whenever we went back and redid all  of that  so you can see that uh the methanol mtve  at a 5050 mixture the the green bars  are looking pretty good for the majority  of these samples really  only sample ten and one need a little  bit of work  so let's go back and optimize our sample  preparation procedure  and see if we can work with sample  number one and sample number 10  and see if we can get these samples  looking good by optimizing our procedure  so using a half gram of lotion bomb or  cream again  adding our co-solvent uh methyl terbutyl  ether methanol  mixture and then vortexing we're going  to do  a step in there where we try and  optimize  time on shaker table so after we add  everything together we're gonna do  no time on shaker table five ten or  fifteen minutes  and then we'll centrifuge it for five  minutes uh take an aliquot of the  supernatant and dry off the solvent  reconstitute it with a different solvent  and then we're going to put that  centrifuging back in and see  if that will start to help with these  two samples  so we'll test this at 0 5 and 10 minutes  before transferring an aliquot into a  filter vial  and injecting that onto the instrument  so these are the results for our  previously outlined experiments  so up top is the bar graph for lotion  number one  and at the bottom the blue one is the  bar  graph for lotion number 10. on the  y-axis is calculated milligrams of cbd  per bottle  and that green dotted line is going to  be the  actually reported value so the the value  that's on the bottle  on our x-axis in the smaller subgroup we  have  no centrifuging five minutes of  centrifuging and  ten minutes and then in the larger uh  sub  portion of the x-axis we have time on  shaker table so no shaker table  five minutes ten minutes and fifteen so  when looking at this data you can start  to see some really interesting  trends going on here so basically  time on shaker table had the most effect  with no time on shaker table having some  of the  data that was largest away from the  actually reported values so overall  centrifuging didn't have much effect  between the  the subsets whether you did no  centrifuging five minutes or ten minutes  so ultimately five minutes on the shaker  table  and no centrifuging was added to our  sample preparation procedure  so our final sample preparation  procedure for these cbd  infused lotion bombs and creams was half  a gram of sample  with five milliliters of our methyl  tert-butyl ether and methanol 50 50  mixture added  sample is vortexed and total dissolved  as much as possible  it will not dissolve all the way for  some of these samples  and then the samples are put on a shaker  table for five minutes  and centrifuged and then an aliquot is  transferred to a vial and the solvent  dried  off then the sample is reconstituted  with solvent  and filtered with a filter vial so this  used a number of sample preparation  techniques including using an extraction  solvent centrifuging drying off the  solvent and reconstituting with a  different one  and filtration  so the analysis of these samples is  pretty straightforward  raptor rkt and 150 by 4.6 millimeter  column is used  with an isocratic method and an overall  five-minute analysis time  the mobile phases include the same  isochronic mobile phases as previously  outlined for  cannabis flower it's important to always  use a guard cartridge when analyzing  real samples to help protect your  analytical column  and improve the lifetime a  representative chromatogram can be seen  for lotion  at the top a bomb sample in the middle  and a cream sample at the bottom so the  cbd is  peak is alluding a little bit after  three minutes  and the overall analysis time for these  is five minutes just to ensure that  everything is eluding off the column  from the matrix  and there's no excessive buildup  so here we have our results from our  final separate sample preparation  method so our percent recovery is  ranging  from 90 to 108 percent  and our percent difference from our  reported value  ranges from 0 to 20.  so in summary it can be beneficial when  potency testing to have  tailored methods for each type of matrix  it can cost time in the beginning to  develop these methods  but by using tailored methods for each  type of matrix  labs can really save instrument time and  ensure that the best quality data is  being obtained  it's also important to remember that  different labs have different needs  and while some labs may be most  interested in saving money on mobile  phase usage  you know others may be most interested  in shortest  methods and highest throughput of  samples  and then finally sample preparation is  an important step in the method  development process  and it's really essential for complex  matrices as we saw for  our lotion bomb and cream samples this  is going to be the key  to keeping instruments up and running  and obtaining reliable and reproducible  data  as well as maximizing the lifetime of  the analytical column  so i'd like to thank you for your time  today and for joining me  and i'd like to open it up to any  questions from the audience  um if you think of a question later feel  free to  uh send me an email i've listed my email  here on the slide

